1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
[Chanting Sanskrit Invocations]
Let us offer our prayers to our Gurus and their Gurus.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000
We choose the primal couple, Sriman Narayana and Lakshmi, the Lords of the Universe.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
May Sriman Venkatanatha, the lion among poets and logicians, the great Vedanta teacher, ever reside in my heart.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
I bow to Sri Vedanta Desika, the recipient of Ramanuja's grace, adorned with knowledge and detachment.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,000
I take refuge at the feet of our Guru, the ocean of mercy, Ramanuja, who deemed everything other than the golden lotus feet of Acyuta as mere straw.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Salutations to Yamunacharya, to Nathamuni, to Nammalvar, and to Sriman Narayana.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Greetings. This video is about a scholar associated with the Sringeri Sharada Peetham,

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:03,000
who was honored and encouraged by them, and specifically about a controversial statement made by him.

9
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:14,000
I am going to translate all of this into English at the end of this video, so please hold on. The initial part will be in Kannada.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Now, as we know, the Sringeri Sharada Peetham is a very famous institution of the Shankara tradition.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Currently, the pontiff there who holds the title of Jagadguru is Sri Vidhushekhara Bharati Swamiji.

12
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
His Guru is also there, but is retired.

13
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Now, there is a scholar associated with this Peetham named Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat.

14
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:59,000
In November 2021, under the "Shaankara Tattva Prasara Abhiyana" organized by the Sringeri Sharada Peetham,

15
00:01:59 --> 00:02:11,000
his lecture was published on their YouTube channel, "Shaankara Abhiyaanam".

16
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:18,000
In this lecture, he makes some highly incorrect and absurd claims. Let's listen to them.

17
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
But before that, let's understand some background about this scholar.

18
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:40,000
He was honored with a prestigious award by the Sringeri Sharada Peetham itself.

19
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:59,000
This is the video that was sent to me, which has been widely shared on WhatsApp.

20
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Here, we can see the Sringeri Acharya honoring him. Let's watch.

21
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:22,000
"Sri Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat..." He might be an Asthana Vidwan of the Peetham, as some say.

22
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:49,000
[Video shows Sri Vidhushekhara Bharati Swamiji honoring him with the "Sri Bharati Tirtha Puraskar" award]

23
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Now, let's listen to the statement he made in his lecture. Listen very carefully.

24
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:18,000
[Suryanarayana Bhat quoting Abhinava Shankara's commentary]
"Therefore, even for a chaste wife (pativrata) who sees many husbands..."

25
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:39,000
[Suryanarayana Bhat continuing quote]
"...those who try to seize the meaning of Rudropanishad to mean other than Samba Parabrahma are great sinners like Ravana who tried to seize Sita."

26
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Look at this! He is quoting the words of Srimad Abhinava Shankaracharya, a commentator on Sri Rudram.

27
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:14,000
And what does this commentator say? That Ramanuja and his followers are "great sinners like Ravana who kidnapped Sita," because they interpret the word "Rudra" as referring to Vishnu.

28
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Now, why did they have to write such things? Even a common person knows who "Rudra" is.

29
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Amarakosha lists "Rudra, Kapardi, Srikantha..." as names of Shiva. Even those who know basic Sanskrit know this.

30
00:05:47,000 --> 00:06:05,000
But it seems Ramanuja did not know this! Because he claims that "Rudra" refers to Vishnu and not Shiva.

31
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:18,000
And this commentator uses the word "Ramanujadayaha" (Ramanuja and others). So, there are others like him too!

32
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:33,000
They all interpret it this way, even though everyone knows it refers to Shiva.

33
00:06:33,000 --> 00:07:12,000
[Suryanarayana Bhat continues quoting Abhinava Shankara]
"...Even if she acts otherwise, her heart is always set on her husband. Similarly, the heart of Rudropanishad is set only on Samba Parabrahma."

34
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:44,000
[Suryanarayana Bhat continues]
"...Those who try to twist it, like Ramanuja, are great sinners like Ravana who kidnapped Sita and tried to woo her in Ashokavana, but failed. Similarly, the efforts of these commentators are futile."

35
00:07:44,000 --> 00:08:00,000
So, according to them, Ramanuja interpreted the word "Rudra" as Vishnu in some commentary and got it wrong.

36
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:14,000
And because of this interpretation, they say the true meaning of the "Rudropanishad" (Sri Rudram) was "abducted" or distorted.

37
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:22,000
But the truth is, Ramanujacharya never wrote any commentary on Sri Rudram or the Rudra Prasna!

38
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Let's see what Ramanuja actually says in his "Vedartha Sangraha" regarding the word "Rudra". He quotes Mahabharata.

39
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:41,000
"Mahabharate ca Brahma-Rudra-samvade Brahma Rudram prati aha..."
In the Mahabharata, in the dialogue between Brahma and Rudra, Brahma says to Rudra:

40
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:53,000
"tavantaratma mama ca ye canye dehasamjnitah..."
"Narayana is the inner self of both you and me, as well as of all other embodied beings."

41
00:08:53 --> 00:09:03,000
"iti rudrasya brahmanas-canyesam ca dehinam parameshvaro narayano'ntaratmatayavasthitah..."
This clearly shows that Narayana is the supreme Lord dwelling as the inner self of Rudra, Brahma, and all other beings.

42
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:16,000
So, to claim that Ramanuja did not know Amarakosha or the conventional meaning of "Rudra" as Shiva is absolutely laughable.

43
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Furthermore, they didn't just criticize Ramanuja. They used the word "Adayah" (and others) to criticize others too. Who could those "others" be?

44
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Well, one of them must be Adi Shankaracharya himself! Because in his "Vishnu Sahasranama Bhashya", look at what he writes.

45
00:09:44,000 --> 00:10:07,000
[Showing text of Vishnu Sahasranama Bhashya]
On the name "Rudra", Adi Shankaracharya interprets it as Vishnu, citing etymology: "As He causes beings to cry at the time of cosmic dissolution..."

46
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:20,000
So, Adi Shankaracharya himself is one of those who interpreted "Rudra" as Vishnu!

47
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:37,000
So, by the logic of "Abhinava Shankara" and Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat, Adi Shankaracharya himself must be a "sinner comparable to Ravana"!

48
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:53,000
This is indeed highly ironic. They are indirectly calling their own foundational Acharya a great sinner.

49
00:10:53,000 --> 00:11:13,000
And this video has over 11,400 views on the official Sringeri channel "Shaankara Abhiyaanam", with 333 likes and zero dislikes!

50
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:35,000
This channel has over 43,000 subscribers, and the comments are full of praises like "Om Namah Shivaya", "Very beautifully explained", etc.

51
00:11:35,000 --> 00:12:01,000
It is highly amusing that these modern followers of Shankara are essentially branding Adi Shankaracharya as a sinner for interpreting Rudra as Vishnu.

52
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Ramanuja has nothing to do with this criticism because he didn't even write a commentary on Sri Rudram. His philosophy simply holds that all words ultimately refer to Narayana as the inner self of all.

53
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:37,000
So if we take this "Abhinava Shankara"'s criticism to its logical conclusion, it directly condemns Adi Shankaracharya.

54
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:53,000
And it's not just the Vishnu Sahasranama Bhashya. Let's look at the Brahma Sutra Bhashya of Adi Shankaracharya.

55
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:07,000
Under the sutra "sākṣād-apy-avirōdhaṃ jaiminiḥ", in the Vaishvanara Adhikarana,

56
00:13:07 --> 00:13:30,000
Shankaracharya validates the etymological interpretation of terms like "Vaishvanara" and "Agni" to ultimately refer to Parabrahma (Narayana), rather than just the physical fire or elemental deity.

57
00:13:31,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Throughout his commentaries on Brahma Sutras, Upanishads, and Bhagavad Gita, Shankaracharya explicitly defines Parabrahma as Narayana. He often interprets conventional terms as referring to Narayana.

58
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:35,000
So, this criticism by "Abhinava Shankara", supported by Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat and Sringeri Sharada Peetham, directly backfires on Adi Shankaracharya himself.

59
00:14:36,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Additionally, they are also criticizing Sayana, another scholar in the Shankara lineage. In his Rigveda Bhashya (10.136.7), Sayana interprets the word "Rudra" as "vaidyutagni" (lightning fire) rather than Shiva.

60
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:54,000
So, Sayana too becomes a "sinner like Ravana" by their standards! It seems they are eager to condemn everyone who doesn't fit their narrow sectarian view.

61
00:15:55,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Now, what is the context of all this? How did this video reach me? I did not go looking for it; someone sent it to me.

62
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:45,000
This seems to have been triggered by a conflict between Madhvas and Shankaras.

63
00:16:45 --> 00:17:10,000
Let's watch this clip from Kahale News, which was recorded in Udupi. Some Madhva ladies are giving a discourse.

64
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:52,000
[Madhva ladies on news channel: "According to Madhva texts like Mani Manjari, a demon named Maniman obtained a boon from Rudradeva and was born as Shankara in Kaladi to spread false doctrines like 'Jagat is illusion' and misguide people..."]

65
00:17:52,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Here, they are quoting from the Madhva text "Mani Manjari" which says Shankara was an incarnation of a demon.

66
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Naturally, the modern followers of Shankara were offended by this.

67
00:18:42,000 --> 00:19:07,000
And they forced these ladies and the matha that hosted them to issue a public apology, which we see here.

68
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:32,000
[News clip showing the ladies apologizing: "We did not mean to offend anyone. We were just quoting from the text... if we hurt anyone's feelings, we apologize."]

69
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:54,000
So, the Shankaras forced them to apologize for quoting their traditional texts.

70
00:19:54,000 --> 00:20:27,000
But what about the Shankaras themselves? They are doing the exact same thing! Their own texts call Ramanuja a great sinner like Ravana, and they are proudly broadcasting this on their official channels.

71
00:20:28,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Isn't this hypocrisy? "What we do is wonderful, but what others do is an atrocity." They demand apologies from others, but propagate vile criticisms against other Acharyas on their own platforms.

72
00:21:19,000 --> 00:22:40,000
[Preparing materials to summarize in English...]

73
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:51,000
A brief summary of what was said in this video. So, it seems that there is a person called Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat, who is associated with Sringeri Sharada Peetham.

74
00:22:51,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Now, this Sringeri Sharada Peetham ran some abhiyana called "Sri Shankara Tattva Prasara Abhiyana", a series of lectures, amongst which Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat delivered a certain lecture, which I have played earlier.

75
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:25,000
There he quotes someone called Abhinava Shankara, who commented on the Rudra Prasna, where he criticizes Ramanuja

76
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:35,000
for interpreting "Rudra" as pertaining to Vishnu. However, that's not the case. Ramanuja did not comment on Rudra Prasna at all, to my knowledge.

77
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:45,000
If you know of any, please let me know. It will be a new discovery, at least for me.

78
00:23:45 --> 00:24:06,000
So, the objection does not fly. Abhinava Shankara, whoever he was, and the presenter, Suryanarayana Bhat, as well as his backers, Sringeri Sharada Peetham and modern-day Shankaras, they were all wrong

79
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:20,000
about this criticism of Ramanuja regarding the misinterpretation of Rudra as Vishnu.

80
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Suryanarayana Bhat further criticizes that Ramanuja did not know Amarakosha because in Amarakosha it is clear that the term Rudra pertains to Parvatipati Shiva.

81
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:56,000
It implies that Ramanuja was such an idiot that he did not know this. So these are the words and the implications of Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat that I have covered in the previous Kannada video; you may look at it at your leisure.

82
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:15,000
So, as I said, no bhashya of Ramanuja exists for Rudra Prasna. And Ramanuja has very clearly stated in Vedartha Sangraha, which also I have quoted in the previous video, where he uses Rudra to refer to none other than Parvatipati,

83
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:32,000
where Brahma and Rudra are discussing with each other, and Brahma tells Rudra, "Look, Rudra, the Antaratma of you and me is Bhagavan Narayana only."

84
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:41,000
So, it is clear that Ramanuja knows what Rudra means, and he interprets Rudra as being Parvatipati. He is not an idiot who does not know the kosha.

85
00:25:42,000 --> 00:26:12,000
And further, this Suryanarayana Bhat and the person he cites, Abhinava Shankaracharya, they both imply that there are other people—using the term "adi", they imply that there are other people who opine the same, who think that—who try to twist the word Rudra to mean something other than Parvatipati.

86
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Well, that includes your own Acharya, Shankaracharya! Because he has commented on the Vishnu Sahasranama Bhashya.

87
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:41,000
Let me try to open it... Sorry, here it is. So in Vishnu Sahasranama Bhashya, it is very clear that according to Shankaracharya, the author of Vishnu Sahasranama Bhashya, Rudra refers to Vishnu, by the magic of etymology.

88
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:55,000
Well, so what we have here is Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat, sponsored by Sringeri Sharada Peetham, and many Shankaras,

89
00:26:55 --> 00:27:26,000
according to them, by the use of the "adi" shabdha, Adi Shankaracharya himself is a "papishtha", a bad sinner, a person comparable to Ravana. So that's what it comes to.

90
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:38,000
And if you object saying that, "No, no, our Shankaracharya never wrote a commentary on Vishnu Sahasranama, that was by some other Shankaracharya," well even so, you can take the Vaishvanara Adhikarana of Brahma Sutra Bhashya.

91
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:53,000
And there it is clear that under the sutra "sākṣād-apy-avirōdhaṃ jaiminiḥ", it is very clear that he is open to etymologically taking other words to refer to Paramatma, whom he identifies explicitly as being Narayana.

92
00:27:53,000 --> 00:28:09,000
He says Narayana is the supreme Lord.

93
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:34,000
So even in Brahma Sutra Bhashya, where he takes the terms "Vaishvanara" and "Agni" to mean Paramatma, whom he calls Narayana, not only in Brahma Sutra Bhashya but also in Bhagavad Gita Bhashya and Upanishad Bhashyas, which were genuinely authored by him, and he separates it from Rudras and Adityas in Bhagavad Gita Bhashya.

94
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:50,000
It is very clear that Shankara falls into the category of people you call sinners, papishthas, being like Ravana who kidnap Sita and so on.

95
00:28:50,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Not only Shankara, you are also criticizing Sayana, who was a Shankara follower, because in Rigveda 10.136.7, he uses etymology to take Rudra to mean vaidyutagni, to mean lightning. So you are criticizing these people. Well, it's nothing to me because they are not my Acharyas, but they are your Acharyas. One wonders how appropriate that is.

96
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:38,000
And what is the context of all this? Well, I showed the context in the previous video. It seems that these ladies here, they quoted, I think, Mani Manjari, some text called Mani Manjari, which is a Madhva text,

97
00:29:38 --> 00:30:10,000
to imply that Adi Shankaracharya was a demon by name Maniman who got a boon from Rudradeva and was born to confuse—put bad ideas in people's heads. How much true that is, you and I are welcome to decide based on the evidence we can muster and based on our unbiasedness.

98
00:30:10 --> 00:30:26,000
Well, these modern Shankaras, led by this person, I think, they forced these people to apologize very profusely. The Shiroor Math, I think, or other Udupi Math which hosted this event,

99
00:30:26 --> 00:30:41,000
was forced to dissociate itself from these lecturers, and they were made to apologize very profusely. I felt sorry for them.

100
00:30:41 --> 00:31:02,000
Well, in that case, one would ask: Sir, isn't this hypocrisy? Because your tradition has texts which compare Ramanuja to Ravana and calls him a papishtha, a sinner, and so on. Is it fair for you to do this and expect others not to do the same?

101
00:31:02 --> 00:31:17,000
Well, if you force these people to apologize, are you going to force this Suryanarayana Bhat and Sringeri Sharada Peetham and your followers, the Shankara followers, to apologize?

102
00:31:17 --> 00:31:33,000
Because they are calling—we don't care, I mean, it is your svabhava to demonize Ramanujacharya, Madhvacharya, whoever, I don't know, to call them papishthas, to call them Ravanas and so on, it doesn't matter to us because it's your svabhava, you are free to do it.

103
00:31:33 --> 00:31:51,000
But don't these other people deserve the same freedom? Don't they also get their freedom to comment about your Acharyas as well? And aren't you concerned about your own Acharya Adi Shankaracharya, Sayanacharya, being called a papishtha by your own Abhinava Shankara, so-called Abhinava Shankara, and probably Asthana Vidwan—I'm not sure, probably Sringeri Sharada Peetham Asthana Vidwan—who was definitely honored by Sringeri Sharada Peetham.

104
00:31:51 --> 00:32:18,000
Who was honored with the award.

105
00:32:18 --> 00:32:37,000
So shouldn't you be upset about these people? That is something you should consider.

106
00:32:37 --> 00:32:55,000
And furthermore, when you say—I found another funny thing in this video which I would like to quote in English and discuss it in English...

107
00:32:56 --> 00:33:01,000
"śruti-smṛti-purāṇānām ālayam karuṇālayam |
namāmi bhagavad-pāda-śaṅkaram loka-śaṅkaram ||"

108
00:33:02 --> 00:33:14,000
So, when you say, "śruti-smṛti-purāṇānām ālayam karuṇālayam namāmi bhagavad-pāda-śaṅkaram loka-śaṅkaram," what do you mean?

109
00:33:14 --> 00:33:39,000
Because according to Adi Shankaracharya, according to Shankara philosophy, shruti is avidya, smriti is avidya, puranas are avidya. All of these are avidya. Just like the Buddhists say, "shruti is avidya, all these astika texts are avidya, they are maya, they mislead people," you also say the same thing.

110
00:33:39 --> 00:33:50,000
In some places, you say it's anuvaada of loka, and the loka is avidya. So according to your philosophy, from your own words, shruti, smriti, and purana are avidya only.

111
00:33:50 --> 00:34:04,000
And according to your siddhanta only, we should say: "śruti-smṛti-purāṇānām ālayam 'havidyālayam' namāmi bhagavad-pāda-śaṅkaram loka-śaṅkaram."

112
00:34:04 --> 00:34:17,000
Please, this is not me making fun of your siddhanta; your siddhanta itself is like that. I am just highlighting what you say. This is not me making fun of it. However, it could be taken in another way as well.

113
00:34:17 --> 00:34:49,000
You can take avidya to mean not a technical term, but to mean actual maleficence, bad intellect, something like that, which is what your lecturer, Sri Hittalli Suryanarayana Bhat, and the person he quoted, Abhinava Shankaracharya, they are implying, and which is what their supporters and followers seem to be supporting. Sringeri Sharada Peetham and all these people who delightfully commented upon his video, who liked, who watched these videos (11,470 views, 333 likes, 43.4k subscribers, 21 comments, all praises).

114
00:34:49 --> 00:35:08,000
They are all endorsing these views.

115
00:35:08 --> 00:35:28,000
Well, they are all endorsing these things. So, it is something for you to consider. These people are actually saying: "śruti-smṛti-purāṇānām ālayam 'havidyālayam' namāmi bhagavad-pāda-śaṅkaram loka-śaṅkaram."

116
00:35:28 --> 00:35:45,000
Not as an accurate presentation of your siddhanta, but in some sort of a derogatory nature, which is not my intent, I should clarify that.

117
00:35:45 --> 00:36:20,000
And you should consider the propriety of saying this shloka when you introduce your Acharya Shankaracharya using "śruti-smṛti-purāṇānām ālayam", because according to your siddhanta, it would mean that you're introducing your Acharya as a house of avidya, of ignorance, of error. But anyway, it's up to you. It is not my siddhanta; it is your siddhanta. You can decide and act however you like.

118
00:36:20 --> 00:36:35,000
In conclusion, I would just emphasize that it is not a big deal for ancient texts to have criticized quite harshly their opponents, and for modern upanyasakas (modern lecturers) to quote the same accurately.

119
00:36:35 --> 00:36:46,000
It's fine. It doesn't mean that Hindu unity is going to get broken.

120
00:36:47 --> 00:37:03,000
Hindu unity, when it comes to anyone attacking Shankaras or Madhvas or Sri Vaishnavas, we are all together, we will fight back together. That doesn't mean that we should stop criticizing each other.

121
00:37:03 --> 00:37:22,000
We should not feel scared about it. Well, for example, in recent times, Skanda, Kartikeya, Subrahmanya is being demoted to a human in Tamil Nadu by Muslims, Christians, and other panelists,

122
00:37:22 --> 00:37:34,000
nastikas, atheists—the Dravida desha is full of atheists—and among the people who are in the forefront of criticizing them, fighting back against those people, are people who don't themselves worship Subrahmanya, but consider him to be a God.

123
00:37:34 --> 00:37:53,000
For example, Dushyanth Sridhar, a Sri Vaishnava, a very famous upanyasaka. So, you don't have to—and I will do the same. I will happily do the same. Anyone attacks Hinduism, I will happily criticize those people and fight back against those people.

124
00:37:53 --> 00:38:03,000
You don't have to worry about that. I will end by quoting a shloka related to me by an elder person, a follower of Kanchi Peetham, which goes like this:

125
00:38:03 --> 00:38:14,000
"parasparavirodhe ca vayam pañca ca te śatam |
anyaiḥ saha virodhe tu vayam pañcādhikaṃ śatam ||"

126
00:38:14 --> 00:38:43,000
"Amongst our quarrels, we are five, you are a hundred. However, when it comes to fighting others, we are a hundred and five." This is from the Mahabharata, where five Pandavas fight the hundred Kauravas, but when they fight exterior enemies like the Gandharvas, they are a hundred and five, they are united.

127
00:38:43 --> 00:39:08,000
